## 11. UPDATE 2026-05-02 — see VJEPA_LLVE_FINDINGS_2026-05-02.md

Sections 1–10 above reflect state as of 2026-04-30. Significant findings since then.
**For current experimental status, design-decision lock-ins, and next-step recommendations,
see `VJEPA_LLVE_FINDINGS_2026-05-02.md` in this directory.**

### Quick-reference: what changed since 2026-04-30

| Topic | 2026-04-30 view | 2026-05-02 view |
|---|---|---|
| v9 architecture story | v9.0 = clean Retinex baseline, then RAFT + V-JEPA temporal heads | v9.0 baseline kept; RAFT and V-JEPA-affinity branches both **closed** as negatives |
| 25 dB ceiling cause | "V-JEPA representation may be cause" | partly metric/protocol artifact (RGB-256 vs RGB-full-frame); also data + decoder limits |
| V-JEPA's role | "central architectural piece, paper centerpiece" | confirmed **load-bearing as dense conditioning** (+~4 dB), but **NOT a usable supervision target** |
| Motion hypothesis | "V-JEPA's pretraining is motion-rich, motion-rich data should help" | no motion-specific V-JEPA benefit detected on current SDSD/static_np under GT frame-difference proxy (caveat: n=14, possibly different on motion-rich datasets) |
| Project narrative | "V-JEPA-grounded LLVE" (overstated) | "V-JEPA dense feature conditioning for LLVE" (honest) |

### Five settled statements (locked 2026-05-02)

1. V-JEPA dense cross-attention is **load-bearing** (~+4 dB vs noJEPA ablation).
2. V-JEPA token affinity supervision is **rejected** (V-JEPA too low-light-invariant).
3. RAFT/image-space warp supervision is **rejected** on SDSD (warp interpolation noise > frame-pair difference).
4. V-JEPA's measured contribution is **motion-neutral** on current SDSD/static_np (uniform ~3-4.5 dB lift across motion buckets).
5. Next high-value work is **NOT** another V-JEPA-side temporal loss/head; the lever is data scale (BVI-RLV) or decoder/photometric improvement.

### Locked next-step plan (per review thread AU7)

1. **DONE 2026-05-02**: write `VJEPA_LLVE_FINDINGS_2026-05-02.md`
2. **DONE 2026-05-02**: this PROGRESS.md pointer
3. **NEXT**: AR2.A — attempt LLVE-STCD external comparison on our 14 indoor seqs (bounded effort, stop if engineering blocks)
4. **DEFERRED**: v9.3-bigdata (BVI-RLV scale-up); only if AR2.A motivates it
